// The one place an xHCI DMA address leaves its span (GitHub issues #623,
// #720). A device span -- from a dma_fixed allocation or a device protocol
// owner -- carries an address the type system proved inside its
// allocation; exporting it as a bus address is the trusted step, and RP1's
// inbound window offset (rp1_dma_pci_offset) is applied here, once. This
// file is a raw mint file (kernel/RAW_MINT_FILES) for exactly this
// function, so that usb_xhci.tkb itself holds no raw site.

fn xhci_span_bus_address(span: borrow DmaDeviceSpan) -> usize !{unsafe} {
    return unsafe { dma_span_address(span) } + rp1_dma_pci_offset;
}
